{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794521926507,"sessionID":"ses_e2e2a8545ffel5iCm3sO3VeatJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1d786cb0010K5IA3UHbZdUqc","sessionID":"ses_e2e2a8545ffel5iCm3sO3VeatJ","messageID":"msg_1d1d776aa0019RPeX5wcHRV8zV","type":"tool","id":"call_49be2135eb6e48e184414869","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"skill_graph_scan","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor","limit":50},"output":"Found 50 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:\n  Line 345: - CLI calls are sent untrusted by default. Mutations (`advisor_rebuild`, `skill_graph_scan`, apply-mode `skill_graph_propagate_enhances`) require `--trusted` or `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED=1`, the maintainer path. Read commands never need it.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tools/skill-graph-tools.ts:\n  Line 22:   name: 'skill_graph_scan',\n\n  Line 125:     case 'skill_graph_scan':\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:\n  Line 88: Two guardrails apply. First, callers bound the CLI call with their own timeout and fail open on expiry or exit `75`. The CLI starts the daemon when the socket is cold and answers from the local scorer when the daemon stays unreachable. A degraded answer is stale, not missing. Second, CLI calls are sent untrusted by default: the mutation commands `advisor_rebuild`, `skill_graph_scan`, apply-mode `skill_graph_propagate_enhances` require `--trusted` (or `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED=1`), which is the maintainer path. There is no MCP transport to fall back to.\n\n  Line 145: A daemon watches every `SKILL.md`, `ROUTER.md` and `graph-metadata.json` under `.skilled/skills/`. When a watched source changes, the daemon schedules an incremental reindex, publishes a fresh generation after the rebuild and invalidates the recommendation cache. It holds a single-writer lease. Explicit trusted mutation paths are `advisor_rebuild`, `skill_graph_scan` and real `skill_graph_propagate_enhances` apply writes (`mode: apply` with `dryRun !== true`). Corrupt-database recovery may also move aside and recreate the database during lazy initialization.\n\n  Line 162: With `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS=true`, `skill_graph_scan` also harvests frontmatter (`title`, `description`, `trigger_phrases`, `importance_tier`, `contextType`) from every markdown file under each skill's `references/` and `assets/` (READMEs excluded) into a `skill_docs` table. The watcher registers those docs so edits re-index the owning skill. Doc phrases score inside the `derived_generated` lane: top-3 docs per skill, tier-weighted, contribution capped at 0.45, so they assist ranking but cannot hard-route alone. Matching recommendations carry an optional `matchedDocs` field (max 3 sanitized skill-relative paths) pointing at the exact doc to open.\n\n  Line 176: Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 45 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n\n  Line 188: | `skill_graph_scan` | Index every `graph-metadata.json` into the SQLite skill graph |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v0.8.0.0.md:\n  Line 36: `skill_graph_scan` harvests `title`, `description`, `trigger_phrases`, `importance_tier` and `contextType` from each skill's `references/` and `assets/` markdown into `skill_docs`.\n\n  Line 89: - **Verify.** Run a trusted `skill_graph_scan` and expect `docs` counters, then use `advisor_recommend` with a doc-specific phrase and expect `matchedDocs`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v0.7.0.0.md:\n  Line 56: CLI calls are untrusted by default. The mutation tools `advisor_rebuild`, `skill_graph_scan` and apply-mode `skill_graph_propagate_enhances` require `--trusted` or `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED=1`, the maintainer path. An untrusted mutation attempt is refused with exit `64`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:\n  Line 746:     || toolName === 'skill_graph_scan'\n\n  Line 823:   skill-advisor skill_graph_scan --trusted --format text\n\n  Line 977:   if (toolName === 'skill_graph_scan') {\n\n  Line 984:       `skill_graph_scan: ${status}`,\n\n  Line 1430:   const scan = await invokeToolPayload('skill_graph_scan', args, timeoutMs, trusted, warmOnly);\n\n  Line 1441:           { step: 'skill_graph_scan', ok: !scan.isError },\n\n  Line 1584:       : validated.tool.name === 'skill_graph_scan'\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md:\n  Line 29: <!-- Keywords: system-skill-advisor, skill-advisor, advisor_recommend, advisor_status, advisor_rebuild, advisor_validate, skill_graph_scan, skill_graph_query, skill_graph_status, skill_graph_validate, skill_graph_propagate_enhances, cross-skill-edges, gate-2-routing, cli-front-door, daemon-cli, legacy-tool-bridge, skill-graph, pi prompt advisor, prompt-time brief, skill advice before the agent handles my prompt, advisor skipped my prompt, advisor skip my prompt -->\n\n  Line 45: - An operator asks about `advisor_recommend`, `advisor_status`, `advisor_rebuild`, `advisor_validate`, `skill_graph_scan`, `skill_graph_query`, `skill_graph_status`, `skill_graph_validate` or `skill_graph_propagate_enhances`.\n\n  Line 77: - `skill_graph_scan`\n\n  Line 121: - Refresh manually at any time with `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted`.\n\n  Line 206: - CLI callers that run `advisor_recommend`, `advisor_status`, `advisor_rebuild`, `advisor_validate`, `skill_graph_scan`, `skill_graph_query`, `skill_graph_status`, `skill_graph_validate` or `skill_graph_propagate_enhances`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:\n  Line 125:     name: 'skill_graph_scan',\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tools/README.md:\n  Line 24: - `skill_graph_scan`, `skill_graph_query`, `skill_graph_status` and `skill_graph_validate` expose the advisor-owned skill graph command surface, and `skill_graph_propagate_enhances` reports or proposes missing inbound `enhances` edges without trusted-caller authority; only real apply mode (`mode: \"apply\"` with `dryRun` not true) requires a trusted caller.\n\n  Line 55: | `skill-graph-tools.ts` | Defines `skill_graph_scan`, `skill_graph_query`, `skill_graph_status`, `skill_graph_validate` and `skill_graph_propagate_enhances`. |\n\n  Line 93: | `skillGraphScanTool` | Descriptor | Registers `skill_graph_scan`. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees