{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794522100509,"sessionID":"ses_e2e2a8545ffel5iCm3sO3VeatJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1da30b1001wKdui9fKL9LO3I","sessionID":"ses_e2e2a8545ffel5iCm3sO3VeatJ","messageID":"msg_1d1d9f148001BUBoVC6YmzHIDd","type":"tool","id":"call_661d649f802541afb29adc8e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/runtime/freshness-contract.md","limit":120,"offset":1},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/runtime/freshness-contract.md, lines 1-120\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Freshness Contract\"\n3: description: \"Formal contract for advisor freshness: trust states, transition rules, consumer obligations, daemon responsibilities plus failure modes.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"freshness contract\"\n6:   - \"advisor freshness\"\n7:   - \"trust state contract\"\n8:   - \"daemon contract\"\n9: importance_tier: \"important\"\n10: contextType: \"implementation\"\n11: version: 0.8.3.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Freshness Contract\n15: \n16: Open this before deciding whether to use, rebuild or fall back from an advisor result, and when a state such as `stale` or `unavailable` needs a caller to act.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Defines advisor freshness trust states, transitions, caller obligations, daemon duties and failure modes.\n25: \n26: ### When to Use\n27: \n28: - Interpreting `live`, `stale`, `absent` or `unavailable` advisor states.\n29: - Deciding whether to use, rebuild or fall back from an advisor result.\n30: - Debugging watcher, cache or rebuild behavior.\n31: \n32: ### Core Principle\n33: \n34: Callers must treat freshness as part of the routing contract, not as diagnostic decoration.\n35: \n36: ### Two Freshness Axes (Do Not Conflate)\n37: \n38: This contract governs **index trust-state freshness** — whether the skill graph the advisor serves is `live`, `stale`, `absent`, or `unavailable` relative to source changes and daemon liveness. That is the daemon's responsibility and it IS refreshed at runtime (rebuild/scan publish a new generation).\n39: \n40: Separately, each skill's derived block carries **derived-content author-time freshness** in `graph-metadata.json` `derived.generated_at`: the time the derived metadata was last generated/synced from source. The scorer's age-haircut decays a skill's derived lane by this value.\n41: \n42: - It is **author-time, not runtime**: `advisor_rebuild`/`skill_graph_scan` re-index the existing derived block without re-stamping `generated_at`.\n43: - Only a derived-content change through the sync path re-stamps it.\n44: - A freshly rebuilt index therefore does NOT reset the derived-content haircut: a skill whose derived metadata is genuinely old stays penalized by design.\n45: - To refresh derived-content freshness, the derived block must actually be re-synced from source.\n46: \n47: ### Key Sources\n48: \n49: - `runtime/lib/freshness/`\n50: - [`daemon-lease-contract.md`](./daemon-lease-contract.md)\n51: - [`tool-ids-reference.md`](./tool-ids-reference.md)\n52: \n53: ---\n54: \n55: ## 2. TRUST STATE VOCABULARY\n56: \n57: The advisor reports one of four trust states in every response that touches the skill graph:\n58: \n59: | State | Meaning |\n60: |---|---|\n61: | `live` | The index is fresh. Source SKILL.md, ROUTER.md plus graph-metadata.json files have not changed since the last build. The recommendation reflects current skill state. |\n62: | `stale` | The index is queryable but source files have changed since the last build. The recommendation may be wrong for skills modified after the last generation bump. |\n63: | `absent` | The index is missing. The SQLite database file does not exist or was deleted. No recommendation can be computed. |\n64: | `unavailable` | The advisor subsystem cannot be reached. Either the daemon is down or a hard error blocks all reads. |\n65: \n66: State source-of-truth: `runtime/lib/freshness/trust-state.ts` plus `runtime/lib/freshness/freshness-detector.ts`.\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 3. STATE TRANSITIONS\n71: \n72: Trust states transition based on three signals: a generation counter, a source-file hash check, plus daemon health.\n73: \n74: ```text\n75:               [build complete]\n76:                     |\n77:                     v\n78:               +---------+\n79:               |  live   |\n80:               +---------+\n81:                 | ^\n82: [source        | |  [advisor_rebuild succeeds]\n83:  file change   | |\n84:  detected]     | |\n85:                v |\n86:               +---------+\n87:               | stale   |\n88:               +---------+\n89:                 | ^\n90: [db file       | |  [advisor_rebuild succeeds]\n91:  deleted]      | |\n92:                v |\n93:               +---------+\n94:               | absent  |\n95:               +---------+\n96: \n97: [any state] --[daemon down OR crash]--> [unavailable]\n98: ```\n99: \n100: Trigger details:\n101: \n102: - `live → stale`: daemon detects a hash mismatch on any `.skilled/skills/*/SKILL.md`, `ROUTER.md` or `graph-metadata.json` file.\n103: - `stale → live`: `advisor_rebuild` completes successfully plus the generation counter advances.\n104: - `live → absent`: SQLite database file is deleted or fails integrity check.\n105: - `absent → live`: `advisor_rebuild` runs from scratch plus succeeds.\n106: - `* → unavailable`: daemon socket unreachable, daemon process not running or unrecoverable internal error.\n107: - `unavailable → *`: subsystem recovers, fresh `advisor_status` call returns a real state.\n108: \n109: ---\n110: \n111: ## 4. CONSUMER OBLIGATIONS\n112: \n113: Every caller that uses an advisor response must inspect `trustState` plus act accordingly:\n114: \n115: | Caller Type | live | stale | absent | unavailable |\n116: |---|---|---|---|---|\n117: | Hook adapter (Claude, OpenCode, OpenCode) | Use recommendation directly | Use with caveat, log staleness | Skip recommendation, defer to keyword matching against `trigger_phrases` | Skip recommendation, fall back to Python shim |\n118: | Direct CLI caller | Use recommendation directly | Call `advisor_rebuild` first if confidence matters | Call `advisor_rebuild`. Do not act on empty result | Wait for subsystem recovery or use the Python shim |\n119: | Python shim (`skill_advisor.py`) | Use native response | Pass through with stale annotation | Compute fallback locally | Compute fallback locally |\n120: | Validation harness (`advisor_validate`) | Run as configured | Trigger rebuild before measurement | Trigger rebuild before measurement | Fail the validate run with clear error |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 121]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/runtime/freshness-contract.md, lines 1-120\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Freshness Contract\"\n3: description: \"Formal contract for advisor freshness: trust states, transition rules, consumer obligations, daemon responsibilities plus failure modes.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"freshness contract\"\n6:   - \"advisor freshness\"\n7:   - \"trust state contract\"\n8:   - \"daemon contract\"\n9: importance_tier: \"important\"\n10: contextType: \"implementation\"\n11: version: 0.8.3.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Freshness Contract\n15: \n16: Open this before deciding whether to use, rebuild or fall back from an advisor result, and when a state such as `stale` or `unavailable` needs a caller to act.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Defines advisor freshness trust states, transitions, caller obligations, daemon duties and failure modes.\n25: \n26: ### When to Use\n27: \n28: - Interpreting `live`, `stale`, `absent` or `unavailable` advisor states.\n29: - Deciding whether to use, rebuild or fall back from an advisor result.\n30: - Debugging watcher, cache or rebuild behavior.\n31: \n32: ### Core Principle\n33: \n34: Callers must treat freshness as part of the routing contract, not as diagnostic decoration.\n35: \n36: ### Two Freshness Axes (Do Not Conflate)\n37: \n38: This contract governs **index trust-state freshness** — whether the skill graph the advisor serves is `live`, `stale`, `absent`, or `unavailable` relative to source changes and daemon liveness. That is the daemon's responsibility and it IS refreshed at runtime (rebuild/scan publish a new generation).\n39: \n40: Separately, each skill's derived block carries **derived-content author-time freshness** in `graph-metadata.json` `derived.generated_at`: the time the derived metadata was last generated/synced from source. The scorer's age-haircut decays a skill's derived lane by this value.\n41: \n42: - It is **author-time, not runtime**: `advisor_rebuild`/`skill_graph_scan` re-index the existing derived block without re-stamping `generated_at`.\n43: - Only a derived-content change through the sync path re-stamps it.\n44: - A freshly rebuilt index therefore does NOT reset the derived-content haircut: a skill whose derived metadata is genuinely old stays penalized by design.\n45: - To refresh derived-content freshness, the derived block must actually be re-synced from source.\n46: \n47: ### Key Sources\n48: \n49: - `runtime/lib/freshness/`\n50: - [`daemon-lease-contract.md`](./daemon-lease-contract.md)\n51: - [`tool-ids-reference.md`](./tool-ids-reference.md)\n52: \n53: ---\n54: \n55: ## 2. TRUST STATE VOCABULARY\n56: \n57: The advisor reports one of four trust states in every response that touches the skill graph:\n58: \n59: | State | Meaning |\n60: |---|---|\n61: | `live` | The index is fresh. Source SKILL.md, ROUTER.md plus graph-metadata.json files have not changed since the last build. The recommendation reflects current skill state. |\n62: | `stale` | The index is queryable but source files have changed since the last build. The recommendation may be wrong for skills modified after the last generation bump. |\n63: | `absent` | The index is missing. The SQLite database file does not exist or was deleted. No recommendation can be computed. |\n64: | `unavailable` | The advisor subsystem cannot be reached. Either the daemon is down or a hard error blocks all reads. |\n65: \n66: State source-of-truth: `runtime/lib/freshness/trust-state.ts` plus `runtime/lib/freshness/freshness-detector.ts`.\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 3. STATE TRANSITIONS\n71: \n72: Trust states transition based on three signals: a generation counter, a source-file hash check, plus daemon health.\n73: \n74: ```text\n75:               [build complete]\n76:                     |\n77:                     v\n78:               +---------+\n79:               |  live   |\n80:               +---------+\n81:                 | ^\n82: [source        | |  [advisor_rebuild succeeds]\n83:  file change   | |\n84:  detected]     | |\n85:                v |\n86:               +---------+\n87:               | stale   |\n88:               +---------+\n89:                 | ^\n90: [db file       | |  [advisor_rebuild succeeds]\n91:  deleted]      | |\n92:                v |\n93:               +---------+\n94:               | absent  |\n95:               +---------+\n96: \n97: [any state] --[daemon down OR crash]--> [unavailable]\n98: ```\n99: \n100: Trigger details:\n101: \n102: - `live → stale`: daemon detects a hash mismatch on any `.skilled/skills/*/SKILL.md`, `ROUTER.md` or `graph-metadata.json` file.\n103: - `stale → live`: `advisor_rebuild` completes successfully plus the generation counter advances.\n104: - `live → absent`: SQLite database file is deleted or fails integrity check.\n105: - `absent → live`: `advisor_rebuild` runs from scratch plus succeeds.\n106: - `* → unavailable`: daemon socket unreachable, daemon process not running or unrecoverable internal error.\n107: - `unavailable → *`: subsystem recovers, fresh `advisor_status` call returns a real state.\n108: \n109: ---\n110: \n111: ## 4. CONSUMER OBLIGATIONS\n112: \n113: Every caller that uses an advisor response must inspect `trustState` plus act accordingly:\n114: \n115: | Caller Type | live | stale | absent | unavailable |\n116: |---|---|---|---|---|\n117: | Hook adapter (Claude, OpenCode, OpenCode) | Use recommendation directly | Use with caveat, log staleness | Skip recommendation, defer to keyword matching against `trigger_phrases` | Skip recommendation, fall back to Python shim |\n118: | Direct CLI caller | Use recommendation directly | Call `advisor_rebuild` first if confidence matters | Call `advisor_rebuild`. Do not act on empty result | Wait for subsystem recovery or use the Python shim |\n119: | Python shim (`skill_advisor.py`) | Use native response | Pass through with stale annotation | Compute fallback locally | Compute fallback locally |\n120: | Validation harness (`advisor_validate`) | Run as configured | Trigger rebuild before measurement | Trigger rebuild before measurement | Fail the validate run with clear error |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 121]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/runtime/freshness-contract.md\",\"limit\":120,\"offset\":1}"},"time":{"start":1794522099889,"end":1794522100509}}}}
